  "title": "Tainan Night Market",
  "indexDescription": "We visited Tainan's night market.",
  "description": "In 2014 we visited Tainan which is located south of the island.  Taipei is in the north.\n\nI wanted to get a feel of the size of Taiwan by comparing it to the size of Washington which I am familiar with. \n\nTaiwan is about 240 x 90 miles. The north south length of Washington State is 240 miles. You get a similar area by taking the seven north south western counties of Washington, from Canada to Oregon. \n\n• Whatcom- 2503 sq miles\n• Skagit - 2019\n• Snohomish - 2196\n• King - 2307\n• Pierce - 1806\n• Lewis - 2436\n• Skamania - 1683\n------\n14,842 sq miles\n\nThis is close to the size of Taiwan which is 13,855 sq miles. \n\nThe population of this region of Washington is about 5 million. Taiwan has a population of 23 million.",
